{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3321","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3321","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3321\",\"parent_revision\":\"9ea166934fa282fbd0ef50c69834aac5b29a0618381209bfce81c506940dbef3\",\"root_revision\":\"9ea166934fa282fbd0ef50c69834aac5b29a0618381209bfce81c506940dbef3\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nMultiple skill files in the development-harness plugin use literal `Agent(subagent_type=\\\"...\\\", prompt=\\\"...\\\")` call syntax as example/instructional code for how to dispatch a subagent \u2014 e.g. `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` (several instances) and `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` (at least two instances). `subagent_type` is the parameter name of Claude Code's own `Agent` tool specifically.\\n\\nThis plugin's own stated design goal (established for a related, already-fixed issue this session \u2014 commit 11082f0eb, \\\"route agent handoffs through the backend, not SendMessage\\\") is explicit cross-harness portability: the plugin's shipped instruction content targets Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Crush, and Kilo. An instruction block written as literal `Agent(subagent_type=...)` syntax is unexecutable verbatim on any harness that doesn't have a tool named `Agent` with a parameter named `subagent_type` \u2014 the same class of problem the SendMessage fix addressed for a different tool, now observed for the dispatch-invocation syntax itself.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: \\\"subagent_type is not a cross harness term, so it would only work for claude code if its written like that.\\\"\\n\\nImpact: any AI harness other than Claude Code attempting to follow this plugin's own instruction content for dispatching a subagent has no literal syntax to execute at the points where `Agent(subagent_type=...)` appears \u2014 it would need to already know (from outside this document) what its own harness's equivalent call looks like, defeating the purpose of providing example syntax at all.\\n\\nNot yet assessed: the full extent of this pattern across the plugin (only implement-feature/SKILL.md and multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md were checked in this session; other skill files likely have the same pattern), and what a portable replacement notation should look like (literal harness-specific syntax vs. an abstract pseudocode description of the dispatch operation) \u2014 left to grooming/planning.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-08-30, while reviewing PR #3286 (#3276) for writing-for-agents compliance; the specific instance was found while checking implement-feature/SKILL.md's tie between dh:dispatch-contract's selection decision and the `subagent_type` parameter name\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ea30412300916b9381e759a31121ef3684b7b6323aa9a59d2d6abb3837219e8b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRaDXqg\"}"}